                <pb facs="0530" n="1730" xml:id="pg1730"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.0221/1–2252</note>
                <head>No. 789<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The United States High Commissioner for
                        Austria (Donnelly) to the
                        Deputy Director of the Office of Western European Affairs (Williamson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-01-22">January 22, 1952.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dear Francis: In the event you have not
                    been advised by the Department of the Army of their recent communications with
                        USFA on the subject of recruiting aliens
                    for the enlistment program in Austria, I attach copies of a recent exchange of
                    wires between Washington and Salzburg on the subject. I am strongly opposed to
                    the operation of this program in Austria and General Irwin
                    is in entire agreement.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Walter</hi></signed></closer>



